# Slack — PR ready for review

Use when the user asks to **Slack** that a **PR is ready for review**, **notify on Slack**, or follow this template after a PR exists (e.g. `gh pr create` succeeded or they supply a PR number / URL).

## Destination (Slack)

Do **not** auto-send to a channel. Use **`AskQuestion`** and wait for the user’s choice.

**Known team channels (choose one, up to 8):**

| Channel | Notes |
|---------|--------|
| `#generative-search-team` | Private |
| `#command-dev-team` | Private |
| `#project-pmroo-ai` | Public |
| `#innovation-squad` | Private |
| `#product-team` | Public |
| `#integration-development` | Public |
| `#project-pmroo-insights` | Public |
| `#vendoroo-text-agent` | Public |

| Situation | **`channel_id` for `slack_send_message`** |
|-----------|-------------------------------------------|
| **Known team channel** | Resolve the chosen `#…` name → **`C…`**. **Do not** default to the user’s DM. |
| **Testing / self** | When the user says **to myself**, **DM me**, **for testing**, **send to me**, or equivalent, use **their** Slack **user** **`channel_id`** (**`U…`**) or an existing **DM** id (**`D…`**) if you already have it from a prior successful send to them. |
| **Someone else / other channel** | When they name another person or channel, resolve **`slack_search_users`** / **`slack_search_channels`** and use that id. **Do not** invent ids. |

The **Slack app / bot** used by Cursor must be **in** the chosen channel (invited) or **`chat:write`** posts will fail—if send fails with **not_in_channel** (or similar), tell the user to invite the app to that channel.

### Resolving a channel name → **`C…`**

1. Try **`slack_search_channels`** with the channel name (with or without `#`). Include **`private_channel`** in **`channel_types`** when the channel may be private.
2. If **no results**, try **`slack_search_public_and_private`** with the channel name and read the **`Channel: #<name> (ID: C…)`** line from a hit.
3. If still unresolved, ask the user for the **channel id** or confirm the channel name in Slack.

Cached private-channel ids (verify with search if send fails): `#generative-search-team` → **`C0AL9JWTX3N`**; `#command-dev-team` → **`C0AH090T6Q4`**; `#innovation-squad` → **`C08EANVU6A0`**.

