## Prerequisite — Google Calendar helper (before Slack confirmation gate)

**Hard gate:** do **not** open the Slack **mandatory confirmation gate** (summary, mentions, destination, calendar line, send) until **Step A** below is complete or the user explicitly skips the meeting.

### Step A — Run GC Meet Helper first (mandatory)

Before any Slack **`AskQuestion`**, run **`y-rules/agent/y-agt-gc-meet-helper.mdc`** end-to-end for the PR in scope:

1. **Step 0 (mode)** — **`AskQuestion`**: **Generate title and description only** / **Create draft event in Google Calendar** / **`other`**.
2. **Discover PR** — unless the user already named PR **#941** / URL.
3. **Draft + approve** title and styled description per y-agt-gc-meet-helper.
4. **Path A (generate-only):** hand off copy-paste into Google Calendar; **stop** — wait for the user to finish the event (time, guests, Meet).
5. **Path B (create draft):** create draft event via Calendar MCP (15 min from now, no guests); return event link; user may edit in Calendar UI.

**Do not** jump to “Is the meeting on your calendar?” or other Slack confirmations in the **same turn** as Step A starts — finish y-agt-gc-meet-helper (or stop at handoff) first.

### Step B — Calendar line decision (after Step A)

Only **after** Step A handoff or draft create, ask whether the PR review meeting is on Google Calendar:

- **Yes — include calendar line** → include **`:calendar: PR review meeting is already on your calendar. Please check it.`** in the Slack draft.
- **Not yet — wait** → **stop**; do not continue to Slack send.
- **No meeting — omit calendar line** → proceed to the Slack confirmation gate without the calendar sentence.

The calendar reminder sentence must **not** appear unless the user confirms the meeting exists.

**When invoked from Task PR flow (`y-git-create-pr.mdc`):** Step A = Task PR step 16 (Google Calendar PR review meeting (see `.cursor/rules/y-rules/git/y-git-create-pr.mdc`)). Step B + Slack gate = step 17 — only after step 16 is satisfied.

