## Message template (required)

**First line:** **`Ready for review: 👀`** — not “PR is ready for review”.

**Labels — plain text only:** **`PR:`**, **`Task:`**, **`Summary:`** in ASCII. No Slack mrkdwn asterisks for “bold” (Cursor **`slack_send_message`** often renders them as italic). No Unicode stylistic bold.

**One line per URL field:** **`PR: `** + URL and **`Task: `** + Jira URL on single lines each; do **not** put the label on one line and the URL on the next.

**Paragraph breaks:** Use **`\n\n`** between **every** block (headline → **`PR:`** → **`Task:`** → **`Summary:`** → optional calendar line → mentions) when building the **`message`** string for **`slack_send_message`**.

**Calendar reminder sentence (optional):** Add after `Summary:` and before mentions **only when** the user confirmed the PR review meeting is on Google Calendar (see **Prerequisite — Google Calendar**):

**`:calendar: PR review meeting is already on your calendar. Please check it.`**

If there is no meeting, or the user has **not** confirmed it yet, **omit** this sentence entirely.

**Template with calendar line (when meeting confirmed):**

```text
Ready for review: 👀
PR: <GITHUB_PR_URL>

Task: <JIRA_BROWSE_URL>

Summary: <One or two short sentences: what the PR fixes, improves, or adds—outcome-focused. No markdown headings in the summary body.>

:calendar: PR review meeting is already on your calendar. Please check it.

<@USER_ID_1>, <@USER_ID_2>, <@USER_ID_3>
```

**Template without calendar line (no meeting, or not confirmed yet):**

```text
Ready for review: 👀
PR: <GITHUB_PR_URL>

Task: <JIRA_BROWSE_URL>

Summary: <One or two short sentences…>

<@USER_ID_1>, <@USER_ID_2>, <@USER_ID_3>
```

**`Summary:`** — Prefer **one line**, **two sentences max**. Keep the summary body roughly **≤ 320 characters** unless the user asks for more. **Do not** paste secrets, tokens, or long internal-only URLs from the PR into **`Summary:`**. Strip checklist / template boilerplate from the PR **Description** when compressing.

**Last line — mentions only:** Do **not** write **`Reviewers:`**. Use **comma + space** between entries. If there is **nobody** to @mention, **omit** the line **or** use a single plain line: **`(No reviewers requested)`** (no **`@`**).

**Example (calendar line included — meeting confirmed by user):**

```text
Ready for review: 👀
PR: https://github.com/Vendoroo/generative-search/pull/807

Task: https://vendoroo-dev.atlassian.net/browse/VAP-2668

Summary: Improves Resiroo when image analysis fails or is empty: we still attach image URLs for context, skip errored vision rows in descriptions, and keep image numbering consistent for partial results.

:calendar: PR review meeting is already on your calendar. Please check it.

<@U08DXPXGN5U>, <@U097377FRLZ>
```

