## Agent workflow (end-to-end)

0. **GC Meet Helper (Step A)** — run **`y-rules/agent/y-agt-gc-meet-helper.mdc`** first: mode → discover PR → draft title/description → generate-only handoff **or** create draft Calendar event. **Stop** after handoff until the user finishes the event. **Do not** open the Slack confirmation gate in the same turn you start Step A.
0b. **Calendar line (Step B)** — after Step A, **`AskQuestion`**: meeting on calendar? (yes / not yet / no meeting). **Not yet** → stop.
1. **Resolve PR** — **`gh pr view <n> --json url,title,body,commits,reviewRequests,assignees`** (or **`gh pr view --json …`** on the current branch). If there is **no PR**, stop and tell the user to open a PR first. (May overlap with y-agt-gc-meet-helper PR discovery — reuse data when already fetched.)
2. **Jira key** — Parse **`VAP-\d+`** from **`git branch --show-current`** (or user message). Build **`Task:`** link. If **multiple** keys appear, prefer the branch key; if unclear, use the first linked ticket from the PR **Description** or ask once.
3. **Summary** — Write **1–2** sentences from **title + Description + commit subjects**; outcome-only; no **`##`**, no unchecked checklist dumps.
4. **Slack user ids** — For each **`reviewRequests`** entry with **`__typename":"User"`**, **`slack_search_users`** (query: **`login`**, shortened handle if your org maps that way, or **email** if GitHub returned one). Collect **`<@USER_ID>`** in GitHub order.
5. **Assemble** — Concatenate with **`\n\n`**; include the calendar sentence **only** if step 0 / confirmation gate confirmed the meeting exists; apply **`\u200bTask:`** only if **`Task:`** still glues to **`PR:`** in Slack.
6. **Resolve destination** — Use the user’s **`AskQuestion`** choice. Resolve the chosen `#…` → **`C…`** per **Resolving a channel name** above. **Override:** if the user clearly asked to send **to me / for testing / DM**, use **their** **`U…`** (or known **`D…`**); if they named **another user or channel**, resolve that id. **Never** use DM as default for “send Slack” or “PR ready”.
7. **Run confirmation gate** — Ask the mandatory questions in **Mandatory confirmation gate (before any Slack send)** and get explicit confirmation on all required items (calendar first when applicable).
8. **Send** — **`slack_send_message`** with **`channel_id`** from step 6 and **`message`** from step 5, only after step 7 is fully confirmed.
9. **Post-send Jira confirmation** — Ask if the user wants to move the Jira task to In Review now.
10. **Jira required fields** — If user confirms Yes, run **[Jira required fields before In Review](#jira-required-fields-before-in-review)** (re-check loop until all ten fields pass).
11. **Transition Jira** — Only after step 10 passes; call **`transitionJiraIssue`**. If user said No at step 9, do not change Jira state.

