## Resolving reviewers (GitHub → Slack)

**Email from GitHub:** Usually unavailable on **`GET /users/{login}`**; optional **`gh api users/<login> --jq '{login,email,name}'`**.

**`slack_search_users`:** Prefer **exact email** match when email exists; else **`login`**; else a **known** short handle (e.g. org suffix stripping **only** if consistently safe). Read **`User ID`** from the Slack result text. **Never** invent **`U…`** ids.

**No Slack match for a user:** For that slot use **plain GitHub `login` or `name`**, or **drop** the slot—**never** a fake **`<@>`**.

**`__typename":"Team"`** in **`reviewRequests`:** There is **no** Slack **`User ID`**. Append the **team `name` or `slug` as plain text** on the same last line after user mentions (e.g. **`<@U…>, my-team-slug`**) **or** omit and tell the user to add the team ping manually—**do not** guess a **`<@>`** for a team.

**Without Slack MCP:** Last line = comma-separated **Slack display names** or **GitHub `login`** (no **`<@>`** unless ids are known).

