## Output vs Slack MCP

- **Copy-paste (default):** Output the filled template in a **fenced code block** for the user to paste into Slack.
- **`slack_send_message`:** Pass the full string as **`message`** (UTF-8 so **👀** is valid). **`channel_id`** = the **confirmed destination** from the confirmation gate. **Every `<@USER_ID>` notifies that user**—only include people who should be pinged. Always run and complete the **mandatory confirmation gate** first.
- After send, always run **Post-send Jira confirmation**, then **[Jira required fields before In Review](#jira-required-fields-before-in-review)** before any transition.

---

## What not to do

- Do **not** post Slack tokens, webhooks, or bot secrets in chat or in this rule file.
- Do **not** paste private emails or secrets into **`Summary:`** or into shared channels unless the user asked.
- Do **not** guess **`U…`** / **`C…`** / **`D…`** ids—resolve via **`slack_search_*`** tools (or ask the user).
- Do **not** send PR-ready pings to a **DM** by default; pick a **known team channel** (or **other**) via **`AskQuestion`** unless the user asked for DM.
- Do **not** open the Slack confirmation gate before **`y-rules/agent/y-agt-gc-meet-helper.mdc`** (Step A) — generate title/description or create draft event first.
- Do **not** send any Slack message before finishing the **mandatory confirmation gate** (Step B + items below).
- Do **not** include **`:calendar: PR review meeting is already on your calendar`** unless Step A is done and the user confirmed the meeting exists on Google Calendar (Step B).
- Do **not** move Jira to In Review automatically after Slack send; always ask, then run the **required-fields checklist** and wait for the user to fill gaps before transitioning.

