## MCP setup and troubleshooting

Slack tools come from the **Slack MCP server**. If **`CallMcpTool`** reports Slack is unavailable, or channel/user search returns nothing while other MCP servers work, fix configuration before falling back to manual paste.

### 1. Enable Slack in `~/.cursor/mcp.json`

Add a **`slack`** entry (alongside trello, google-calendar, etc.):

```json
"slack": {
  "url": "https://mcp.slack.com/mcp",
  "auth": {
    "CLIENT_ID": "3660753192626.8903469228982"
  }
}
```

**Reload Cursor** after editing (Command Palette → **Developer: Reload Window**, or restart).

### 2. Connect OAuth

**Settings → MCP → Slack → Connect** and approve workspace access. Workspace admins may need to approve the Slack MCP app once.

### 3. Server name in tool calls

Depending on how Slack is loaded, the MCP server identifier may be:

| Source | Server id for **`CallMcpTool`** |
|--------|----------------------------------|
| Entry in **`~/.cursor/mcp.json`** | **`user-slack`** |
| Cursor **Slack** marketplace plugin | **`plugin-slack-slack`** |

Either works when connected. If one fails, try the other before giving up.

### 4. Bot must be in the channel

Invite the Cursor Slack app to the **chosen channel** if **`slack_send_message`** fails with **not_in_channel**.

### 5. Resolving a private channel when channel search is empty

Several known destinations are **private** (`#generative-search-team`, `#command-dev-team`, `#innovation-squad`) — **`slack_search_channels`** often returns no hits even when the bot can post. Use this order:

1. **`slack_search_channels`** with the channel name and **`channel_types`** including **`private_channel`**
2. If empty → **`slack_search_public_and_private`** with the channel name and read **`Channel: #<name> (ID: C…)`** from a hit
3. Cached ids (verify with search if send fails): `#generative-search-team` **`C0AL9JWTX3N`**, `#command-dev-team` **`C0AH090T6Q4`**, `#innovation-squad` **`C08EANVU6A0`**

